{
  "date": "2026-10-26",
  "scope": "Actual compound queue replay for lease, failure/expiration, cancellation, progress/yield and completion, with exact task/reader/receipt effects on errors; continuation-root preservation derived from the actual progress contract. Complete outer dispatch, mixed histories, admission, retirement, cache/quarantine and ownership remain open.",
  "properties": {
    "release_current/finish/failed/cancelled": "Select the attempt of the same current task, release it before a requested task update, preserve all peer readers and describe the exact completed prefix on error. Failed releases; expiration and cancellation retain readers. no_release_preserves_readers derives reader preservation for either task success or local failure.",
    "complete": "Validate receipt.task_id, release the current reader, mark the task completed, then install the submission receipt and append to commits. Every error identifies the correct preceding effects; success returns the same borrowed task ID.",
    "register_current/leased": "Install the supplied lease/generation before registering the input selected from the same updated task. Reader-registration failure retains the completed task update. Input cloning preserves canonical content and finite observations under the existing primitive contract.",
    "progress_readers/progress_current/progress": "Snapshot the selected task lease; extend its reader roots using event.input_ref before updating the task. Yield releases its reader before the task change. Failures retain exactly the completed reader prefix; successful results return the borrowed task ID.",
    "queue_transition_roots": "Derive same attempt identity from the actual cloned lease under string_content_contract, then show that a successful non-yielding progress of an existing valid reader keeps every prior root at its original position, protects a non-null new input and preserves every peer reader."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Coordinator invokes the actual verified compound functions. No new I/O or persisted-format change. Lookup uses existing borrowed indexing and String identities. Completion clears its derived deadline only after receipt success; a receipt error leaves that already-quarantined cache unreconciled. Native quarantine/cache conformance is still an explicit boundary. Malformed missing reader-table paths return defined errors. No newly demonstrated valid-API bug or measured zero-overhead claim.",
  "boundaries": [
    "Existing twenty audited serde primitives, String ordering and Value clone/observation assumptions remain. No new primitive, opaque type, Value law or admitted straw operation.",
    "The continuation-root derivation explicitly requires the existing ENV-STRING-KEY string_content_contract. Character equality alone is not silently promoted to opaque logical String identity.",
    "Success/error relations describe compound in-memory replay, not atomic rollback or a complete WAL business fold. Callers must quarantine partial states and rebuild before reuse.",
    "Outer event kind/arguments/yield flag, stale attempt admission, global order allocation, ReaderRetired retain/callback, derived caches, native recovery/lock/run binding, complete root extraction and cross-log/catalog GC ownership remain unfinished.",
    "Four new unit regressions target malformed-state/error-prefix boundaries. They are not witnesses that valid public API histories create those malformed states. Existing installed-wheel workflows provide integration coverage, not an end-to-end formal proof."
  ],
